WEBVTT

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.990
Can you imagine...

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:16.200
...a life in which you could
never touch the one you love?

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.460
He takes the life of whatever he touches.

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:21.880
That was the curse the witch put on him.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:23.750
His own mother has
distanced herself from him.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.090
His friends have called him a monster.

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:31.260
Even strangers have spoken of him as the
Death incarnate that dwells in the forest.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:32.930
And yet,

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:36.180
he doesn't feel the least bit lonely.

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:10.900
Episode 11

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:11.190
Th-This weighs a ton.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:12.990
Thanks for doing the heavy lifting.

00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:20.700
Do you really think this storeroom could
hold some clue to breaking his curse?

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:23.330
Couldn't we at least let
the servants handle this?

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:27.710
We don't know what Mother
would say if she found out.

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:31.300
And we won't know whether there's
any kind of lead unless we look for it.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:37.510
Why would you bother getting
yourself all covered in dust...

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:40.260
I knew it! You <i>are </i>fond of him!

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:43.060
Am I not good enough for you, Viola?!

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:44.850
You are such a royal pain...

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:49.400
First off, Walter, wasn't it you who said
you wanted to help and followed me here?

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:50.520
Well, yeah!

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:55.280
If I could find some clue to his curse,
I'd be one step ahead of him.

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:57.780
No, not one step.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:58.780
Two!

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:01.490
Not the dreaded number two!

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:10.170
The servants' logbook?

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:14.880
Dear Brother, straighten up in here, okay?

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:16.470
Viola! Viola!

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:21.220
Mother...

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:27.020
What could you possibly
have done to get that dirty?

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:29.190
And I see you're wearing
that same old outfit...

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:31.690
She's a disgrace. Get her out
of those clothes right away.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.200
Come in.

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:44.700
Is this better?

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:45.870
Yes.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:49.040
From now on, you should
always dress like this.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:50.040
But...

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:53.630
...long skirts just aren't my style.

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:56.550
It's a vast improvement over
those childish outfits of yours.

00:03:56.550 --> 00:04:00.760
One day you will be
married into another family.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:03.180
Try not to do anything that would bring
shame to our noble family name.

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:09.350
You're always saying that, Mother!

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:11.400
Can't I wear the clothes I like?

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:14.070
Can't I live my own life?

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:19.150
No, you can't.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:26.040
I can't take it anymore!

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:31.960
That sharp-tongued, flat-chested old hag
with her creepy make-up! She's so cruel!

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:35.300
I think your badmouthing
is what's cruel here.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:37.710
I'm badmouthing her because
I can't say it to her face!

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:40.470
Oh, this totally sucks.

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:42.890
I won't stop crying unless
Rob gives me a hug!

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:44.760
What are you crying for?

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.060
You look good in that dress.

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:49.230
Huh?! Quit trying to console me!

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:51.060
I was paying you a compliment...

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:54.360
I don't think this is that
big of a problem.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:59.690
Your Grace? I believe this is more than
just a problem with her clothes.

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:02.530
If you say so, Alice,
then you're probably right.

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:04.280
What's with the flip-flopping?

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:06.740
So, it's all settled.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.870
I'm moving in as of today.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:10.830
I brought my luggage and everything.

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:12.830
Well, I won't let you, so go home.

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:15.710
You mustn't make Mother
and everyone else worry.

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:18.630
I don't want to live under
the same roof as that woman!

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:21.550
If you're going to say that, Dearest
Brother, then why don't <i>you </i>go back home?

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:24.220
I would if I could!

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:27.640
Okay then, how about I come here
to work as one of your servants?

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:29.720
I can clean and do laundry,

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:32.140
I could even be your court musician!

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:35.060
I could get good at cooking if I studied!

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:37.820
I could even come here as Rob's
pet if push came to shove.

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:39.530
What do you think, Dearest Brother?

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:40.940
I think you're being too persistent.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:43.490
Hey Alice, what do you say?

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:46.870
Talk him into it, pwease?

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:50.370
Pwease? Pwease?

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:47.820
Your Grace...

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:50.370
That's not fair, Viola, in so many ways!

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:54.790
If I lived here, I could forget about the
family's standing and do what I like.

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:59.210
I wouldn't be under anyone's thumb,
and I could wear whatever I want.

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:00.420
Forgive the intrusion.

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:01.920
OMG, it's Rob!

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:03.680
Indeed I am.

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:04.550
Well, well!

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:08.180
Who is this young lady who
has fled here from her castle?

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:10.020
Why, it's you, Lady Viola.

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:12.270
What a lovely dress you're wearing.

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:13.480
R-Really?

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:15.650
M-Mother dressed me in it!

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:17.190
If you like the way I look, Rob,

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:19.980
then maybe I'll wear something
like this sometimes when I visit.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:23.030
Um, yeah, that's what I'll do. Definitely!

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:29.080
Are you really going to spend
the night in my room?

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:31.750
Yeah. I decided not to run away,

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:33.410
but I did bring my luggage and all,

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:36.040
so I thought it might be fun if the two
of us had another girls-only party.

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:39.000
Also, I have something to give you, Alice.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.710
Well, I wonder what it could be.

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:43.590
Hey! I let myself in.

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:45.760
Cuff! What are you doing here?!

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:48.260
Oh, you're here too, Viola?

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:53.180
So, you've been waiting here on your own
without telling anyone you were coming?

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:55.270
Can't I come over without an invitation?

00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:56.520
No, you can't.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:59.610
If you're going to come over,
you should at least say so in advance!

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:01.650
That's what's called having good manners!

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:03.240
Oh, it's no big deal.

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:07.030
Since we're all here, why don't the three
of us have a girls-only party tonight?

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:09.410
Well Alice, if you're okay with it,
then I guess I am, too...

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:11.530
Cuff, are those the clothes
you're going to sleep in?

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.910
I brought some extra pajamas with me.
Shall I lend you a pair?

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:14.790
Really?

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:16.080
Well then, let me borrow them!

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.370
Hey! Not so fast!

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:19.500
Don't you have any tact?!

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:20.590
Tact? What's that?

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:24.130
How are they?
My pajamas are kind of on the big side,

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:26.630
so I think they might be
a little loose on you...

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:28.430
Yep, looking good!

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:30.220
Just a little tight in the chest, eh?!

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:31.640
Oh my, how soft!

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:33.270
Lady Viola?

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:38.560
Did the lady of the house give you any
trouble about having spent Christmas here?

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:40.690
Oh, you mean my mother?

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:44.610
She was really pissed because
both Walter and I went out.

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:50.410
It seems she was particularly hard on him.

00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:51.830
I see.

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:54.660
It's good for Walter
to get chewed out a little.

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:56.540
The same applies to Dearest Brother.

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:59.920
Whichever of them becomes
the family heir has got to be strong.

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:02.460
The two of them are
hopeless as they are now.

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:04.840
You may be saying that now,
but you know it's not true.

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:07.260
When I asked you before if you
liked your dearest brother,

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:08.840
you said, "I do."

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:12.640
No! What I was trying
to say was, "I do <i>not</i>!"

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:14.140
You! Quit smiling!

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:15.180
Hey! I've got it!

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:18.770
Since this is a girls-only party and all,
let's talk about love. Okay?

00:08:18.770 --> 00:08:21.020
You have such an obvious way
of changing the subject.

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:23.110
I-I-I-I wouldn't say that.

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:25.690
So, Cuff? Is there somebody you like?

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:30.110
I don't like talking about my love life.

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:31.780
Oh, come on! It's no big deal.

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:33.950
Who was your first love?
Have you ever been in a relationship?

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:35.450
Have you kissed anyone before?

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:36.450
Huh?

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:39.750
Quit it!

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:41.790
Oh, I can't take anymore! I give up!

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:47.670
I think <i>you're </i>the one with the obvious
way of changing the subject!

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:48.630
Yeah, you're right.

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:50.090
Huh?!

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:51.800
Lady Viola?

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:56.060
Come to think of it, didn't you say
you had something to give me?

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:59.310
Oh, yeah, that's right.

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:03.020
I thought there might be some clue to
breaking the curse somewhere in my house.

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:06.610
And after searching through
a lot of stuff, I found this.

00:09:06.610 --> 00:09:11.030
It's the servants' logbook from around
the time Dearest Brother got cursed.

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:12.160
Oh, my!

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:14.570
I don't know whether it'll be of any use,

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:16.990
but I thought I'd give it
to you anyway, Alice.

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:19.290
Why, thank you.

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:21.960
I think His Grace will be
very pleased as well.

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:25.790
My mother's handwriting...

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:29.880
Hey, Cuff. You've gotten quiet all
of a sudden. Is something wrong?

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:31.260
Yeah, on second thought,

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:34.800
maybe it wasn't a good idea to come over
and spend the night without asking first.

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:37.470
What's with the delayed reaction and all?!

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:40.100
Aw, come on! It's not like I was being
serious when I criticized you.

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:41.810
Oh, my, how soft!

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:43.020
What a relief!

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.030
This bed's too small.

00:09:50.030 --> 00:09:52.360
Well then, why don't you go
and sleep in the mansion?

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:54.610
No, I'd better stay here.

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:58.290
You're still a child, Viola,
so there's safety in numbers.

00:09:58.290 --> 00:10:02.160
However you look at it, you're the child.
In terms of your mental age.

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:07.500
Wh-What's with you, Alice?

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:08.880
Yeah, you're sure in a good mood.

00:10:22.310 --> 00:10:23.640
I see...

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:26.810
Perhaps...

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:28.570
...it's time for me to act.

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:43.910
It appears Viola didn't
come home last night.

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:46.120
S-So it would seem.

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:47.670
Where exactly has she been going?

00:10:48.920 --> 00:10:52.300
I haven't forgiven you for
what happened at Christmas.

00:10:52.300 --> 00:10:54.010
Answer me, Walter.

00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:56.130
W-Well, uh...

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:04.640
So, what is it you wanted
to talk about, Daleth?

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:07.270
Well, I'm not going to
make a fuss about...

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:09.520
...the humans you brought
to the witches' sabbath.

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:11.610
Hmm... So, are you going to...

00:11:11.610 --> 00:11:13.360
...confess your love to me or something?

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:14.820
Of course not.

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:16.150
I'd like to ask you a favor.

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:18.160
Like, to take your hand in marriage?

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:23.700
I hope you keep stubbing your toe against
the corner of a closet until you die.

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:26.250
What's got <i>your </i>panties in a knot?

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:28.040
My request is a simple one.

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:31.590
I'd like you to deliver your
"pals" a message.

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:32.710
My pals?

00:11:34.050 --> 00:11:36.260
What's that you're reading?

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:42.640
It's an old servants' logbook
from the main residence.

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:44.980
Lady Viola gave it to me
thinking it might have...

00:11:44.980 --> 00:11:47.520
...some information that
could help break the curse.

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:48.600
Oh.

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:51.440
Well, the binding
certainly looks familiar.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:53.570
Some of the pages were
written by you, Rob.

00:11:53.570 --> 00:11:54.730
See?

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:55.740
Hmm...

00:11:56.650 --> 00:12:02.530
My cursive's so bad I can't make
out what I wrote apart from my name.

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:05.700
That's just like you, Rob.

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:08.710
What did the others write about?

00:12:08.710 --> 00:12:11.750
It's mostly about work.

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:15.840
Even now you could learn
a lot from reading it.

00:12:15.840 --> 00:12:17.920
For instance, my mother wrote...

00:12:19.010 --> 00:12:25.270
"Two women in white nun's habits came to
the mansion. I hadn't seen them before."

00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:27.230
What's the matter?

00:12:27.230 --> 00:12:28.640
Rob?

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:30.400
Do you recall seeing...

00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:35.070
...two women in white nun's habits at the
mansion while my mother was still alive?

00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:37.860
No, I don't.

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:43.870
You... know who I am?

00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:48.460
My mother must have been writing
about Daleth and someone else.

00:12:48.460 --> 00:12:50.040
Why would witches...

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:51.580
Ooh, there's Alice!

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:53.000
No, Zain! Don't!

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.500
Alice and Rob are on
their breaks right now.

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:58.170
I can at least pop in to say hi, can't I?

00:12:58.170 --> 00:12:59.630
Howdy, Rob!

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:01.720
Zain, welcome!

00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:04.010
Did you come by yourself?
That's kind of unusual.

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:05.010
Yeah, I guess.

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:09.020
As long as I'm here seeing Alice and all,
I've got a message for you from Daleth.

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:10.390
Daleth?

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:13.650
Oh, you mean the skeleton lady that
took roll at the witches' sabbath?

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:15.860
I told you she was our leader, didn't I?!

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:17.690
That's a heck of a way to remember her!

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:19.240
Oh, she's your leader? Sorry.

00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:21.860
Zain? What did Daleth say?

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:25.700
She said, "Let's be friends."

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:27.200
What's that supposed to mean?

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:31.290
Our "friends" stay out of one another's
business, so what she's saying is...

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:33.420
...she wants you to have
nothing more to do with us.

00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:35.960
That's exactly the opposite
of what the word means!

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:37.630
I don't have any other leads.

00:13:37.630 --> 00:13:41.510
So, if I have nothing to do with you guys,
what's to become of my curse?

00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:43.300
Hey, you're barking up the wrong tree.

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:48.720
Well, no matter what Daleth says,
Cuff and I will still help you.

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:52.190
It'd be a shame if you couldn't break
your curse and stayed a <i>virgin </i>for life.

00:13:52.190 --> 00:13:53.940
What the heck are <i>you </i>laughing at?!

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:57.520
So... what are you reading, Alice?

00:13:57.520 --> 00:14:00.190
An old logbook from the main residence.

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:02.650
Oh, really? Anything useful in it?

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:06.200
I just started reading it,
so I really couldn't say.

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:09.540
I plan to read it at my leisure
and learn what I can from it.

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:10.500
I see.

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:12.660
Let me know if you find out anything.

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:13.790
I certainly will.

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:16.290
Well, now that I've seen Alice,

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.130
let's go have some fun if you're game.

00:14:18.130 --> 00:14:18.960
All right?

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:19.960
Sure!

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:23.470
I'll bring you some tea later on.

00:14:23.470 --> 00:14:25.510
Thanks, Alice.

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:27.390
Okay, see you then.

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:30.810
You don't have to do that, you know!

00:14:30.810 --> 00:14:33.230
Hey! Let me feel the excitement, too!

00:14:39.150 --> 00:14:42.190
Aw, jeez! You're noodling around too much!

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:44.030
Oh, quit whining! There's no harm in it.

00:14:44.030 --> 00:14:45.910
Let me play it how I feel it.

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:48.200
It don't have to be pretty to be art!

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:50.910
Yeah, I know, but...

00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:52.040
All right! Perfect!

00:14:52.040 --> 00:14:55.370
Let's see. If I was going
to name this song...

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:58.340
...how does "I Dedicate This Love
to You, Alice" sound?

00:14:58.340 --> 00:14:59.750
Nuh-uh, no way!

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:00.800
Why not?

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:02.380
"Why not?" Because...

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:05.470
...I should be the only one
to tell Alice he loves her!

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:10.680
Oh, man! That was <i>so </i>cringeworthy.

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:13.480
You're the one who can't be true
to your feelings in front of Cuff.

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:14.810
How uncool is that?

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:17.480
I'm always true to my desires.

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:19.150
That's not what I mean!

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:23.940
Anyhoo. Now for Part Two!

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:26.400
Would you at least call it the
Second Movement or something?!

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:28.240
Hey now, loosen up a bit!

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:36.040
Rob, have you seen Zain?

00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:37.500
Zain?

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:41.340
Yeah. I left him alone for a bit,
and he went off somewhere.

00:15:41.340 --> 00:15:43.760
Now I can't find him.

00:15:43.760 --> 00:15:47.340
Come to think of it, when I was making
my rounds of the second floor just now,

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:51.260
I did hear someone climbing the stairs.

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:52.350
Really?

00:15:52.350 --> 00:15:54.770
I wonder if he's exploring
the mansion or something.

00:16:00.190 --> 00:16:01.520
I can't find it anywhere.

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:08.740
Go tell your pals, "Let's be friends."

00:16:08.740 --> 00:16:13.120
Also, that girl Alice has gotten
her hands on an old logbook.

00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:13.950
A logbook?

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:16.870
Yes. A logbook from that mansion.

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:19.620
There may be something
written about me in there,

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:21.840
so I'd like you to quietly get rid of it.

00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:24.670
Now hold on. They're my pals.

00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:27.470
I can't just get rid of something
that belongs to them.

00:16:27.470 --> 00:16:30.640
Well, this isn't exactly a request...

00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:31.890
...it's a threat.

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:39.810
I could take her from you, you know.

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:50.070
Zain?

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:51.410
Is something the matter?

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:55.660
That logbook...

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:59.210
Well now, this is pretty awkward.

00:16:59.210 --> 00:17:03.080
To be perfectly honest,
Daleth asked me to get rid of it for her.

00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:08.470
She used Cuff as leverage to threaten me.

00:17:08.470 --> 00:17:11.010
I would do anything for Cuff.

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:15.470
But not this. This is wrong.

00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:20.890
There's something in there that
Daleth wants to keep secret.

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:24.900
I have no idea what it is
or what page it's on.

00:17:24.900 --> 00:17:26.110
But...

00:17:26.110 --> 00:17:28.320
...I'm sure the information
will be useful to you.

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:33.320
Go ahead and burn it. I don't mind.

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:35.120
Huh?!

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:37.740
I couldn't cause you or Cuff any trouble.

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:41.080
I'd hate it if something bad
happened to Cuff,

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:43.710
and if someone had used Alice
as leverage to threaten me,

00:17:43.710 --> 00:17:46.500
I'm sure I would've done the same thing.

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:51.260
You guys are dear friends to me,
so go ahead and burn it.

00:17:57.760 --> 00:17:59.560
Aw, what the hay?

00:17:59.560 --> 00:18:02.140
Guess I'd better strip to
the waist and help you out.

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:03.230
Bet you'd like <i>that</i>, you perv!

00:18:03.230 --> 00:18:05.310
<i>You're </i>the perv!

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:08.820
Daleth is watching you and Alice.

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:11.150
I bet she's watching us right now.

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:15.070
She uses all sorts of "eyes" in the human
realm to conduct surveillance.

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:17.620
Surveillance?

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:20.540
That's right. But she can't listen
in on what we say.

00:18:20.540 --> 00:18:23.290
So, what I'm about to tell you now
is strictly confidential.

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:27.170
There <i>is </i>a way to prevent Cuff from harm
without destroying this logbook.

00:18:27.170 --> 00:18:28.840
Just one, in fact.

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:30.170
Really?

00:18:30.170 --> 00:18:33.170
Yeah. Just watch.

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:37.430
I don't much care for my magic,
so don't ask me to go into details.

00:18:37.430 --> 00:18:39.850
Cuff and you are the
only ones I've shown it to.

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:48.270
Well, since Daleth is watching us now,
then naturally she's watching this, too.

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:50.400
As long as I've got this tiny scrap,

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:53.490
I can restore what I just
disintegrated at any time.

00:18:53.490 --> 00:18:56.950
In other words,
the logbook still "exists."

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:02.790
I'll hang on to this until Daleth
has removed her surveillance.

00:19:02.790 --> 00:19:03.910
Is that all right with you?

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:05.370
Y-Yeah.

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:08.960
Please, don't tell anyone
about my magic, okay?

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:10.300
Well then...

00:19:10.300 --> 00:19:14.470
Since Daleth's watching, we've got to
convince her the logbook's been destroyed.

00:19:14.470 --> 00:19:16.970
Okay, pretend you're sad!

00:19:16.970 --> 00:19:19.640
Huh?! Um, is this... good?

00:19:19.640 --> 00:19:22.060
All right, I guess this'll do.

00:19:22.060 --> 00:19:24.140
For making me play your sick errand boy,

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:27.650
I should at least get to squeeze
one of your boobs, Sister Skeleton.

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:30.650
You sure say some outrageous stuff
when you know she can't hear you.

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:34.740
So, you took the logbook, Your Grace?

00:19:34.740 --> 00:19:36.240
Um, yeah.

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:38.990
I felt like reading it, so I went
ahead and borrowed it.

00:19:38.990 --> 00:19:40.240
I'll return it when I'm done.

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:42.490
All right. What a relief!

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:46.620
It wasn't in my room,
so I thought I'd lost it.

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:48.710
I can't believe I just lied to Alice.

00:19:48.710 --> 00:19:52.050
But I promised to keep Zain's secret.

00:19:52.050 --> 00:19:53.510
Hey, Alice?

00:19:55.970 --> 00:19:58.890
I'll protect you no matter what.

00:20:01.350 --> 00:20:04.180
I'll protect you no matter what.

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:07.560
Oh, my! From what?

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:12.900
Well, I'm not sure, but if somebody
came along and tried to hurt you...

00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:15.490
You're such a wonderful,
reliable person, Your Grace.

00:20:15.490 --> 00:20:17.450
Oh, you're already in danger!

00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:21.320
I'm really happy and all,

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:25.620
but please don't go very far, Your Grace.

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:28.460
Of course, I'll stay by your side.

00:20:28.460 --> 00:20:31.040
Why don't we have some tea for now?

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:37.630
I wonder what Daleth's
trying to keep secret.

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:39.800
The reason why I was cursed?

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:42.180
The reason why the witch
who cursed me died?

00:20:42.180 --> 00:20:45.180
Or how to break this curse?

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:47.350
This puzzle's full of missing pieces.

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:48.940
But...

00:20:48.940 --> 00:20:51.440
I will find a way to break this curse.

00:20:51.440 --> 00:20:53.190
For my sake and Alice's as well...

00:21:09.710 --> 00:21:12.080
Does he think he's making fun of me?

00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:16.630
He really ticks me off.

00:21:16.630 --> 00:21:17.880
But that's okay.

00:21:17.880 --> 00:21:19.930
I saw what I wanted to see.

00:21:19.930 --> 00:21:22.550
So, I'll leave things the way
they are for now.

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:34.980
It seems that fate
and karma really do exist.

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:36.780
Don't you think so?

00:21:39.950 --> 00:21:42.950
Don't you, Sharon?

00:23:15.120 --> 00:23:16.120
Here's your mail!

00:23:16.120 --> 00:23:17.580
Oh!

00:23:17.580 --> 00:23:19.040
Thank you.

00:23:22.460 --> 00:23:23.670
Hmm?

00:23:23.670 --> 00:23:25.930
This is...

00:23:25.930 --> 00:23:29.390
This is the first time I've ever
gotten a letter from Mother.

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:30.930
I wonder what she wants.

00:23:34.430 --> 00:23:36.230
What is it?

00:23:36.230 --> 00:23:37.810
It's a summons.

00:23:37.810 --> 00:23:39.810
She said she needs to talk,
so she wants me to...

00:23:39.810 --> 00:23:41.690
...go see her at the main house
in a week's time.

00:23:43.190 --> 00:23:46.030
"Together with the Duke..."
